From 61b665a5b163a1a6dd5ff2e62547c6f36d12d292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:47:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gl: EmbedLite's swap chain reuses its surfaces, three of them

SwapChain::Acquire compared the pooled surfaces' color space with the one
requested (sRGB), but CreateShared() makes a factory without color spaces,
like the EGLImage one, use Display. Every Acquire emptied the pool, so each
frame created a framebuffer, texture and EGLImage and destroyed the
previous ones, which the embedder could still be drawing (white views,
the driver crash in ~MozFramebuffer) and which took seconds per frame on
the PowerVR SGX530. On the N950, 91 frames instead of under 25 in the same
swipe test, two framebuffers in turn.

The pool holds three surfaces: the embedder draws the front buffer on its
own render thread, which may still be at the previous frame when the next
one starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gfx/gl/GLScreenBuffer.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gfx/gl/GLScreenBuffer.cpp b/gfx/gl/GLScreenBuffer.cpp
index 60d53c91854e..f95654ef8be9 100644
--- a/gfx/gl/GLScreenBuffer.cpp
+++ b/gfx/gl/GLScreenBuffer.cpp
@@ -28,7 +28,11 @@ UniquePtr<SwapChainPresenter> SwapChain::Acquire(
     const auto& existingDesc = mPool.front()->mDesc;
     auto newDesc = existingDesc;
     newDesc.size = size;
-    newDesc.colorSpace = colorSpace;
+    // CreateShared() makes a factory without color spaces use Display; a
+    // request for another space must not empty the pool on every frame.
+    newDesc.colorSpace = mFactory->SupportsCspaces()
+                             ? colorSpace
+                             : gfx::ColorSpace2::Display;
     newDesc.transferFunction = transferFunction;
     if (newDesc != existingDesc || !mPool.front()->IsValid()) {
       mPool = {};
@@ -150,7 +154,9 @@ SwapChain::SwapChain()
        // #1646073.
       mPoolLimit(
 #ifdef MOZ_EMBEDLITE
-          2
+          // The embedder draws the front buffer on its own render thread,
+          // which may still be at the previous frame when the next starts.
+          3
 #else
           kIsAndroid ? 4 : 0
 #endif
-- 
